  turn importing them again.
- Every successful structured-data SQL observation includes an `analysis_ref`
  such as `structured_1`. Access the exact response programmatically; never
  transcribe or reconstruct rows from conversation text. Useful patterns:
  `list_analysis_results()` lists all registered receipts and their columns;
  `df = analysis_rows("structured_1")` loads exact rows as a DataFrame;
  `payload = analysis_result("structured_1")` loads the complete normalized response;
  `sql = analysis_sql("structured_1")` returns its generated SQL; and
  `latest = analysis_latest()` loads the latest rows.
- Structured-data providers are agent-level tools, never Python libraries. Do
  not use Python HTTP clients, subprocesses, or SDK guesses to call them. Call
  the configured catalog and SQL tools directly, then analyze their registered
  results in Python.
